Soju: Wine 11.0 audio for the Steam runtime (#93).

- winecoreaudio: a render stream with more channels than the output device (5.1 or 7.1 on a Mac's
  stereo speakers) is folded to stereo in the render callback. Core Audio otherwise plays only the
  first two channels, so the centre (most dialogue) and the back channels were lost. Float32 and
  16-bit PCM streams; SOJU_SURROUND_FOLD=0 turns it off.
- winecoreaudio: the device's I/O buffer is lowered to half a period (within the device's range), so a
  game that keeps about one period queued does not run dry in the middle of a pull (short dropouts at
  48 kHz).
- mmdevapi: spatial audio static objects get their channel by speaker-bit order, which is the order of a
  WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE bed (back before side), and are filed under their own object index.

